     <svg:desc>12§display§Q=CV§png§600§FALSE§</svg:desc>
    </draw:frame><text:span text:style-name="T17">). FETs take advantage of this physical phenomenon: as opposed to a BJT, where there is a non-negligible current which flows into the device from the base, a FET, or field-effect transistor, attempts to isolate it’s control terminal from the active device. </text:span></text:p>
