       </draw:frame>Figure <text:sequence text:ref-name="refFigure6" text:name="Figure" text:formula="ooow:Figure+1" style:num-format="1">4</text:sequence>: (a) hypothetical semiconductor device, (b) operation as a capacitor, (c) current flow as a result of the electron difference <text:span text:style-name="T16">(Razavi)</text:span></text:p>
     </draw:text-box>
    </draw:frame></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P15"><text:tab/>This isolation is achieved by taking advantage of the electric field produced by a capacitor. Looking at figure <text:sequence-ref text:reference-format="value" text:ref-name="refFigure6">4</text:sequence-ref>(c), we can control the current through the material by adjusting V_1, which in effect, adjusts the resistance through the device. </text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P15"><text:tab/><text:span text:style-name="T18">A common type of FET is the MOSFET (Metal-oxide Semiconductor FET). </text:span></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P14"><draw:frame draw:style-name="fr3" draw:name="Frame8" text:anchor-type="as-char" svg:width="5.5791in" draw:z-index="16">
